<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rio Grande</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Río Bravo del Norte</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rio Grande is a river that rises in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> and flows south through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, then forms the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>. Its upper valley was the heart of Pueblo country and of Spanish New Mexico. After Texan independence the lands north of its lower course were disputed with Mexico until 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rio-grande.jpg" alt="Rio Grande" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Glysiak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rio_Grande_in_Big_Bend_NP.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
